Tiny Death Star for webOS (HP TouchPad) — an apkenv port
=======================================================

This is the Android build of LucasArts / NimbleBit's **Star Wars: Tiny Death
Star** (1.4.1) running *natively* on webOS. There is no ACL (OpenMobile's full
Android runtime) and no Dalvik: apkenv is a slim shim — a gingerbread bionic
linker loaded as a library, a fake-JNI layer, a webOS SDL/PDL backend, and a
per-engine module that plays the part of the game's Android Java host.

The engine is **Cocos2d-x 2.0.4** (lib/armeabi-v7a/libgame.so). The module
(apkenv/modules/cocos2dx.c) answers its Java contract: the GL surface and frame
loop, touch, text rasterization (Cocos2dxBitmap, done here with FreeType), the
writable data directory, and device facts. Sound is the game's own FMOD, which
plays through apkenv's OpenSL ES shim (apkenv/compat/opensles.c).

WHAT WORKS
----------
  Portrait, full panel (768x1024 rendered, rotated onto the 1024x768 screen).
  The LucasArts loading screen, the tutorial, building the tower, touch.
  Music and sound effects (FMOD, 24000 Hz stereo).
  Saves persist across restarts and reinstalls.

WHAT IS MISSING, AND WHY
------------------------
  Anything that needs a network or an account: the Disney/Playdom social
  features (visiting friends' towers), in-app purchases, ads, push
  notifications, Facebook / Google+. The shim reports the device as offline,
  a state the game already handles. The social SDK still tries to reach its
  servers in the background and fails harmlessly.

LAYOUT OF THIS APP DIRECTORY
----------------------------
  apkenv            The host binary (native ARM ELF). On launch it self-locates,
                    cd's here, picks the game under android/, and runs it.
  appinfo.json      webOS app manifest (type:pdk, main:apkenv).
  icon.png          Launcher icon.
  README            This file.

  libs/webos/       Harvested Android 2.3 bionic libc/libm/libstdc++/liblog/libz,
                    loaded by apkenv's own linker, plus the TouchPad's libEGL.so.

  android/          tinydeathstar.apk is shipped whole: the engine reads its
                    native libraries and all of its assets straight out of it.
                    apkenv.env holds launch settings (see below).
    extras/         tinydeathstar-splash-768x1024-rgb.raw — the game's own
                    res/drawable-xhdpi/splash.png, pre-scaled raw RGB (bottom row
                    first), shown while the tower loads.

RUNTIME-WRITABLE DATA (the app directory is read-only at runtime)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
  /media/internal/.apkenv/tinydeathstar.apk/app_data/
                                            the save (UserDefault.xml plus the
                                            game's own json caches) and FMOD's
                                            sound banks, which the game copies out
                                            of the apk on first launch (~11 MB).
  /media/internal/apkenv-com.apkenv.tinydeathstar.log
                                            this app's stdout/stderr, rewritten on
                                            every launch.

LAUNCH SETTINGS (android/apkenv.env)
------------------------------------
  APKENV_PTHREAD_STACK_CLAMP=1    FMOD asks for thread stacks that are too small
                                  for glibc; raise them.
  APKENV_SPLASH_RGB / _SIZE       The loading screen payload above.

SOURCE AND NOTES
----------------
